From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bullhead-linux <kaiwalyakhasnis57@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:29:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8994: give the PCIe aux RCGs a parent
 map

From oneplus2-mainline (github.com/luvingiane/oneplus2-mainline, patch 0027, GPL-2.0); the same GCC on MSM8992.

Like usb3_phy_aux_clk_src (patch 0024): the PCIe aux clock sources use P_XO
in their frequency table but have no parent_map, so nobody can set their
rate (clk_set_rate() dereferences NULL) and the aux clock stays as the
bootloader left it, which does not set PCIe up. CAF runs it at 1.01 MHz
(pci-msm.c msm_pcie_clk_info). XO is the first entry of gcc_xo_gpll0_map.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c
index 12957f06d..57352091b 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8994.c
@@ -862,6 +862,8 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 pcie_0_aux_clk_src = {
 	.cmd_rcgr = 0x1b00,
 	.mnd_width = 8,
 	.hid_width = 5,
+	/* without a map, clk_set_rate() dereferences NULL */
+	.parent_map = gcc_xo_gpll0_map,
 	.freq_tbl = ftbl_pcie_0_aux_clk_src,
 	.clkr.hw.init = &(struct clk_init_data){
 		.name = "pcie_0_aux_clk_src",
@@ -921,6 +923,8 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 pcie_1_aux_clk_src = {
 	.cmd_rcgr = 0x1b80,
 	.mnd_width = 8,
 	.hid_width = 5,
+	/* without a map, clk_set_rate() dereferences NULL */
+	.parent_map = gcc_xo_gpll0_map,
 	.freq_tbl = ftbl_pcie_1_aux_clk_src,
 	.clkr.hw.init = &(struct clk_init_data){
 		.name = "pcie_1_aux_clk_src",
